# Alfred writes its live preferences bundle straight into this directory (its
# sync folder points here), so some of what appears is runtime state, and some of
# it is content that must never reach a public repo.

# --- snippets: deny by default, allow by name ---------------------------------
#
# Snippet collections are the highest-risk content in this bundle: they are free
# text the human types into over years, and one of them turned out to hold a live
# OpenAI API key (plus personal and corporate email addresses in another).
#
# A blacklist is the wrong shape here — it only protects against the collections
# someone already thought of, so a collection created next month gets committed
# before anyone looks at it. Deny everything and list the collections that have
# been read and judged safe. Adding a line here is a deliberate act; forgetting to
# add one costs nothing.
#
# The bundle is the live directory, so an ignored collection still works in
# Alfred exactly as before — it just stays local.
Alfred.alfredpreferences/snippets/*
!Alfred.alfredpreferences/snippets/Ascii Art/
!Alfred.alfredpreferences/snippets/Currency Symbols/
!Alfred.alfredpreferences/snippets/Dynamic Content/
!Alfred.alfredpreferences/snippets/Emoji Pack/
!Alfred.alfredpreferences/snippets/Funny Quotes/
!Alfred.alfredpreferences/snippets/Mac symbols/
!Alfred.alfredpreferences/snippets/Pragma/

# Per-machine settings, keyed by a hash of the machine. Alfred writes one
# subdirectory per Mac that has ever opened this bundle — appearance, clipboard
# retention, per-machine hotkeys. Tracking them means every machine fights over
# every other machine's file.
Alfred.alfredpreferences/preferences/local/

.DS_Store
